2.1 Layered Independent Testing Strategy

- Contract Testing (Pact, Spring Cloud Contract): QA enforces consumer/provider pact verification in CI/CD before cross-team integration occurs.
- API & Messaging (Playwright, Karate, Kafka Schema Reg): QA validates schema evolution, serialization, idempotency, and retries independently of supplier UI.
- Integration & Virtualisation (WireMock, Hoverfly, Testcontainers): QA provides stubbed environments so third-party dev teams can test without waiting on other vendors.
- Scenario / E2E (Playwright TypeScript): QA executes targeted E2E validation strictly for critical business flows (e.g., UC Payment Calculations).
- Observability (OpenTelemetry, Dynatrace): QA continuously monitors canary and production deployments to validate real-world operational health.

2.2 Risk-Based Prioritisation Framework
Testing rigor is determined by assessing Impact of Failure against Architectural Complexity:
* Critical Risk (Financial / Policy Impact e.g., Entitlement Calculations): Requires QA-driven dual-write automated reconciliation, golden-master characterisation tests, and performance gate execution.
* High Risk (High-Volume Asynchronous Events e.g., Change of Circumstance): Mandates schema registry validation, consumer-driven contract checks, and chaos injection (network latency/circuit breakers).
* Medium/Low Risk (Isolated CRUD Capabilities): Assured via automated API, contract, and schema validation scripts running in CI/CD pipelines.

2.3 Aggregating Granular Evidence into Overall Outcomes
Granular test results roll up into automated Quality Gates to prove end-to-end business integrity:
1. Traceability Mapping: Test execution outputs automatically map back to DWP GDS Service Standards and user stories within Jira/Azure DevOps.
2. Automated Data Reconciliation: Dual-run comparison tools validate that legacy baseline outputs match extracted microservice responses down to individual data fields.
3. Synthetic Transaction Monitoring: OpenTelemetry distributed tracing across service boundaries provides real-time verification of full business transactions in pre-production and production.


SECTION 3: SHARED QUALITY GOVERNANCE & UPDATED DEFINITION OF DONE (DoD)

As the independent QA partner, we establish shared testing standards, test harnesses, and automated quality gates that external development teams must satisfy prior to deployment.

3.1 Multi-Vendor Quality Enablement & Governance
* QA-Provided Test Harnesses: We supply external developer teams with standardized test libraries, contract registries, and mock stubs (WireMock) to accelerate local verification.
* Objective Quality Gates: Pipeline gates automatically enforce quality criteria, providing objective pass/fail metrics without subjective disputes between suppliers.
* Cross-Supplier Quality Coaching: QA leads conduct Communities of Practice (CoP) to onboard third-party developers to DWP contract standards and executable BDD specifications.

